.\" Manual page for hydrogen-group-viewer
.TH HYDROGEN-GROUP-VIEWER 1 "2026-10-31" "nntp2sql (beta 0.50)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hydrogen-group-viewer \- browse the newsgroups stored in an nntp2sql database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hydrogen\-group\-viewer
.RB [ \-\-db\-type
.IR "sqlite" | "mysql" | "postgres"
.RI [ CONNECTION ]]
.br
.B hydrogen\-group\-viewer \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hydrogen\-group\-viewer
is a GTK4 program that lists every newsgroup in the
.B groups
table of an nntp2sql database: its name, the estimated article count, and the first and last article
numbers. Fill the table with
.B nntp2sql \-\-list\-groups
to see the whole server's group list.
.PP
It reads SQLite, MySQL/MariaDB and PostgreSQL databases and starts each with a connection string that
works on a default local installation, so it can be opened and used immediately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-db\-type " \fITYPE\fR [\fICONNECTION\fR]"
Start on the given backend with an optional connection string.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and the default connection strings.
.SH USING THE WINDOW
.TP
.B Backend dropdown
SQLite, MySQL / MariaDB or PostgreSQL. Each remembers its own connection string while the program runs.
.TP
.B Database dropdown, Detect databases
Lists every database with the nntp2sql tables (for example
.BR news0 ,
.BR news1 ).
The first one is opened automatically; choose another to load it.
.TP
.B Connection box, Open / Reload
Type a connection string and press Enter or click the button. The forms are the same as for
.BR isotope\-viewer (1).
.TP
.B Filter box
Shows only groups whose name contains the text (case-insensitive).
.TP
.B Column headers
Click to sort by name, article count, first or last article number.
.PP
Loading runs in the background, so the window stays responsive with lists of over 100,000 groups.
.SH BUGS AND LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
The article count is an estimate (last \- first + 1) until headers have been downloaded for a group,
and it can be far too high on servers with sparse article numbers.
.IP \(bu 2
The program shows every group in the table; it does not show only groups that have articles. Use
.BR isotope\-viewer (1)
for that.
.IP \(bu 2
Connection strings are not remembered between runs.
.IP \(bu 2
PostgreSQL is the least exercised backend.
.SH ICON
The program has its own icon, a card listing newsgroups as an indented hierarchy with a hydrogen-atom badge, named
.BR hydrogen-group-viewer .
On Linux and BSD, GTK finds it in the icon theme (installed under
.IR prefix /share/icons/hicolor ,
with the matching
.B .desktop
file in
.IR prefix /share/applications ),
or next to the program in an
.B icons
folder when run from a build directory. On macOS the Dock icon is set while the program runs. On Windows the
window icon comes from the same icon theme and the executable's own icon is compiled in from
.BR icons/hydrogen-group-viewer.rc .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nntp2sql (1),
.BR isotope\-viewer (1)
